OL,3,ABritish army told to stop non-essential
OL,4,Atraining exercises to save money
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe Army has been told to stop
OL,7,F"non-essential" training exercises to
OL,8,Fsave money, according to a defence
OL,9,Fsource.
OL,11,FIt will continue to train soldiers
OL,12,Fpreparing to be deployed or on
OL,13,Fdeployments - such as units sent to
OL,14,FEstonia, the Falklands or Cyprus.
OL,16,FBut units back in the UK and who are
OL,17,Fnot preparing for a specific deployment
OL,18,Fhave been told to cut back on
OL,19,Fcollective training exercises due to
OL,20,Ffinancial pressures.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG7/39
